## G-20 fix confirmed at the SQL level (T-04/T-05, against local SQLite,
## same fixture as rfcs/handoffs/evidence/baseline-02.log)

1500 rows seeded into check_results at checked_at=2020-01-01 (same
fixture as the pre-fix baseline). New per-batch loop (BATCH_SIZE=100):
select 100 eligible ids -> archive that exact batch -> delete that exact
batch by id -> repeat until empty.

rounds=15 archived_total=1500 deleted_total=1500 remaining=0
PASS: archived_total == deleted_total, table fully drained

Compare to the pre-fix baseline: archived_count=1000, deleted_count=1500,
remaining=0 (500 records deleted with no archive copy). The denominator
that mattered — archived vs. deleted — now matches exactly, at every
batch boundary, not just in aggregate.

## T-09a — archive_to_r2 = 0 on a class requiring archival (added 2026-07-28
## after review, rfcs/handoffs/02-retention-scope.md Build step 4)

$ cargo test -p noye-core --locked db::retention::tests
test db::retention::tests::check_results_and_incidents_require_archival ... ok
test db::retention::tests::audit_logs_does_not_require_archival ... ok
test db::retention::tests::an_unrecognized_table_does_not_require_archival ... ok
# exit code: 0 (16 retention tests total, up from 13)

`run_cleanup` now checks `requires_archival(&policy.table_name) &&
!policy.archive_to_r2` before entering the batch loop for that policy,
and skips with a `console_error!` diagnostic rather than deleting.
`requires_archival` itself (pure, host-tested above) is the only new
decision logic; the skip-and-report control flow was not exercised
against a live D1 environment, for the same reason noted below for
T-06/T-07.

## What remains unverified (honest accounting, per evidence/README.md)

- **T-06** (forced archive failure -> zero records deleted for that
  batch) and **T-07** (aborted pass then successful pass -> exactly
  once each): guaranteed by the code's control flow (archive_batch is
  called and `?`-propagated *before* delete_by_ids in every loop
  iteration; a failed batch is never partially deleted), but not
  exercised against a live D1 + R2 fault injection. No Wrangler/D1
  environment was available in this environment.
- **RETENTION_BATCH_SIZE = 100**: chosen from the commonly-cited D1
  per-statement bound-parameter ceiling, not confirmed against a live
  D1 instance. See the constant's doc comment in retention.rs and the
  "Stop and report" clause in rfcs/handoffs/02-retention-scope.md —
  if a live check finds a different true limit, lower the constant; the
  archived-set-equals-deleted-set property does not depend on its exact
  value.
